1
00:00:01,262 --> 00:00:04,308
[hammer tapping]

2
00:00:04,439 --> 00:00:05,875
- Based on the number of taps,

3
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:07,964
it should be coming
from this direction!

4
00:00:08,095 --> 00:00:09,270
- Up there!

5
00:00:10,923 --> 00:00:13,926
- [Hiraku] Something big
is headed here.

6
00:00:14,057 --> 00:00:15,145
What is that thing?

7
00:00:15,276 --> 00:00:16,407
A dragon?

8
00:00:16,538 --> 00:00:18,714
- No, it's a wyvern!

9
00:00:18,844 --> 00:00:20,411
- It can't be!

10
00:00:20,542 --> 00:00:23,414
[intense music]

11
00:00:23,545 --> 00:00:25,721
[wyvern roaring]

12
00:00:27,810 --> 00:00:30,987
["Flower Ring" by Shino Shimoji
and Aya Suzaki plays]

13
00:01:58,466 --> 00:02:01,251
[intense music]

14
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:12,480
[wyvern roaring]

15
00:02:12,610 --> 00:02:15,570
[all grunting]
[wind howling]

16
00:02:25,188 --> 00:02:27,103
- We must defend, Lu!

17
00:02:29,366 --> 00:02:32,500
[barrier cracking]

18
00:02:35,067 --> 00:02:36,243
[Lea gasping]

19
00:02:36,373 --> 00:02:37,809
- Hurry, we need to
put out the fires!

20
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:39,985
[all panting]

21
00:02:40,116 --> 00:02:41,813
- This is bad.
- Yeah.

22
00:02:41,944 --> 00:02:43,293
Should we attack?

23
00:02:43,424 --> 00:02:45,817
I'm not sure we can
pierce its barrier.

24
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:55,566
[wyvern growling]

25
00:03:01,485 --> 00:03:03,357
[light humming]

26
00:03:03,487 --> 00:03:04,793
[Hiraku gasping]

27
00:03:04,923 --> 00:03:07,796
[light humming]

28
00:03:11,669 --> 00:03:14,846
[energetic rock music]

29
00:03:22,332 --> 00:03:24,204
- Crush him!

30
00:03:33,125 --> 00:03:34,388
- No way!

31
00:03:37,129 --> 00:03:38,522
[Hiraku growling]

32
00:03:45,616 --> 00:03:47,923
[wyvern thudding]

33
00:03:50,186 --> 00:03:52,057
[Lu gasping]

34
00:03:53,581 --> 00:03:56,105
- [Lea] We managed to
put out all the fires.

35
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:57,976
There was some damage
to the crop fields,

36
00:03:58,107 --> 00:03:59,630
but all of the buildings
are fine.

37
00:03:59,761 --> 00:04:01,110
- [Hiraku] I see.

38
00:04:05,419 --> 00:04:07,943
It looks like I managed
to take it down.

39
00:04:08,073 --> 00:04:10,293
Are there a lot of
these creatures?

40
00:04:10,424 --> 00:04:12,426
- There are some places
where they live,

41
00:04:12,556 --> 00:04:14,689
but running into one of
them that's this large

42
00:04:14,819 --> 00:04:16,821
is a very rare occurrence.

43
00:04:16,952 --> 00:04:18,432
- Is there any possibility

44
00:04:18,562 --> 00:04:21,348
that someone sent this
wyvern here to attack us?

45
00:04:21,478 --> 00:04:22,958
- No, I don't think so.

46
00:04:23,088 --> 00:04:25,439
Even if this wyvern was
under someone's command,

47
00:04:25,569 --> 00:04:28,050
they wouldn't send such a
rare and valuable creature

48
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:30,095
off on its own to attack.

49
00:04:30,226 --> 00:04:33,011
It's most likely a wild
creature acting alone.

50
00:04:33,142 --> 00:04:34,230
- [Hiraku] I see.

51
00:04:34,361 --> 00:04:36,276
Then I guess we can safely say

52
00:04:36,406 --> 00:04:38,974
that this was nothing more
than a rare incident.

53
00:04:39,104 --> 00:04:40,236
[all sighing anxiously]

54
00:04:40,367 --> 00:04:42,194
By the way...
- What is it, Hiraku?

55
00:04:43,805 --> 00:04:45,807
- Is it okay to eat this?

56
00:04:46,634 --> 00:04:47,896
[cheerful music]

57
00:04:48,026 --> 00:04:50,246
- [Lu] Wyvern meat
is said be a delicacy.

58
00:04:50,377 --> 00:04:52,379
In fact, it is said that
there was once a king

59
00:04:52,509 --> 00:04:55,469
who sent his army into a
den of wyverns to hunt them

60
00:04:55,599 --> 00:04:57,949
and bring them back for
the king to taste for himself.

61
00:04:58,080 --> 00:05:00,169
- [Tia] Great story, Lu,
but I'm pretty sure

62
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:02,563
that ended with all of them
getting burned to death

63
00:05:02,693 --> 00:05:05,392
and then swallowed whole
by the wyverns, so...

64
00:05:05,522 --> 00:05:06,567
[all exclaiming excitedly]

65
00:05:06,697 --> 00:05:08,264
- Here's the meat in question.

66
00:05:08,395 --> 00:05:12,007
This is a wyvern round steak,
grilled with spices.

67
00:05:13,487 --> 00:05:16,228
I wrapped the breast meat
in leaves and steamed it.

68
00:05:17,708 --> 00:05:20,363
And for the tail meat,
I made a stew with vegetables.

69
00:05:20,494 --> 00:05:21,886
[Lu humming in delight]

70
00:05:22,017 --> 00:05:23,584
- I thought it would be
really tough and gristly,

71
00:05:23,714 --> 00:05:26,195
but this meat,
it's super tender and juicy!

72
00:05:26,326 --> 00:05:28,153
- And to think, a regular
knife couldn't even

73
00:05:28,284 --> 00:05:30,330
pierce its skin,
but now it's so soft!

74
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:34,377
- This delicacy is just as
delicious as it looks!

75
00:05:34,508 --> 00:05:36,423
- [Lu] I can't understand you.

76
00:05:36,553 --> 00:05:38,338
- This broth tastes amazing!

77
00:05:38,468 --> 00:05:42,124
Every bite of meat I take has
more flavor than the last!

78
00:05:42,254 --> 00:05:44,648
[all humming in delight]

79
00:05:44,779 --> 00:05:48,435
- Hey, you think you could have
blocked Hiraku's spear?

80
00:05:48,565 --> 00:05:50,306
- No, not even close.

81
00:05:50,437 --> 00:05:53,440
That attack pierced a
three-layer barrier
from a wyvern,

82
00:05:53,570 --> 00:05:56,921
and then blew right through
its chest like it was nothing.

83
00:05:57,052 --> 00:05:58,880
- [Lu] Maybe it was
a stroke of luck

84
00:05:59,010 --> 00:06:01,361
that Kuro and the dogs
were who we ran into first

85
00:06:01,491 --> 00:06:02,579
when we came here.

86
00:06:02,710 --> 00:06:04,929
- [Tia] Yeah, you're right.

87
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:06,148
- What's the matter?

88
00:06:06,278 --> 00:06:07,758
Did I not get all the bones?

89
00:06:07,889 --> 00:06:10,413
- No, it's just we're blessed
to enjoy our meals

90
00:06:10,544 --> 00:06:11,458
in good health.

91
00:06:11,588 --> 00:06:12,546
- That's right.

92
00:06:12,676 --> 00:06:14,156
We thank fate for smiling on us.

93
00:06:14,286 --> 00:06:15,679
- It's no big deal!

94
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:17,246
- [Tia] This one's
delicious, too!

95
00:06:17,377 --> 00:06:18,682
- [Lu] It really is!

96
00:06:23,339 --> 00:06:24,775
[menacing music]

97
00:06:24,906 --> 00:06:27,169
- [Grattz] You say
a wyvern was taken down?

98
00:06:27,299 --> 00:06:28,649
Enough of these jokes!

99
00:06:28,779 --> 00:06:30,694
- No, the report we
received is true.

100
00:06:30,825 --> 00:06:31,826
- Impossible!

101
00:06:31,956 --> 00:06:33,393
One of those things drawing near

102
00:06:33,523 --> 00:06:36,134
requires that we mobilize
our entire military force!

103
00:06:36,265 --> 00:06:38,006
There's no way...

104
00:06:38,136 --> 00:06:40,312
- He was attacked from the
ground and killed in two hits.

105
00:06:40,443 --> 00:06:41,618
- Absurd!

106
00:06:41,749 --> 00:06:43,403
- Enough of these jokes!

107
00:06:43,533 --> 00:06:44,839
- [Beezel] It's true.

108
00:06:44,969 --> 00:06:46,797
- [growls] We can't fight that!

109
00:06:46,928 --> 00:06:49,931
And we just finished getting
this year's budget approved!

110
00:06:50,061 --> 00:06:50,888
- [Grattz] No...

111
00:06:51,019 --> 00:06:51,976
It's a joke, right?

112
00:06:52,107 --> 00:06:53,587
- [Beezel] Stop saying that.

113
00:06:53,717 --> 00:06:56,328
Now, before panic begins to
spread among our citizens,

114
00:06:56,459 --> 00:06:58,940
it's our job as the generals
to handle this.

115
00:06:59,070 --> 00:06:59,897
- [Randan] I've got it!

116
00:07:00,028 --> 00:07:00,942
Let's resign!

117
00:07:01,072 --> 00:07:02,334
- [Beezel] Please don't.

118
00:07:02,465 --> 00:07:04,902
Don't run away
from this, Randan!

119
00:07:05,033 --> 00:07:07,818
[intense music]

120
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:11,343
- [Dryme] Did you see it, Gucci?

121
00:07:11,474 --> 00:07:14,216
- Yes, I saw it
with my own eyes.

122
00:07:14,346 --> 00:07:15,870
- And what do you
think would happen

123
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,655
if I were to receive
such an attack?

124
00:07:18,786 --> 00:07:20,962
- It would pierce
cleanly through you.

125
00:07:21,092 --> 00:07:24,182
- What do we do?

126
00:07:24,313 --> 00:07:26,228
- It would be foolish to attack.

127
00:07:26,358 --> 00:07:29,100
- [Dryme] Yes, definitely.

128
00:07:34,062 --> 00:07:35,367
[Hiraku humming thoughtfully]

129
00:07:35,498 --> 00:07:37,326
- The wyvern meat was
every bit as delicious

130
00:07:37,457 --> 00:07:40,460
as it was said to be,
but if I'm being honest,

131
00:07:40,590 --> 00:07:43,245
there's still one thing that
was missing from the meal.

132
00:07:43,375 --> 00:07:44,333
[Lu squealing excitedly]

133
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:45,552
- Are we going to start now?

134
00:07:45,682 --> 00:07:47,336
- Is it finally time?

135
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:48,729
- Huh?

136
00:07:48,859 --> 00:07:50,034
Yeah.

137
00:07:51,122 --> 00:07:52,776
We're making alcohol!

138
00:07:52,907 --> 00:07:54,474
[all gasping excitedly]

139
00:07:54,604 --> 00:07:56,388
If we're making alcohol
out of grapes,

140
00:07:56,519 --> 00:07:58,390
then it's going to be wine.

141
00:07:58,521 --> 00:08:00,958
Apparently, wine exists
in this world.

142
00:08:01,089 --> 00:08:04,135
So everyone was excited and
quickly harvested the grapes.

143
00:08:04,266 --> 00:08:06,311
Now all that's left is to
squash the grapes

144
00:08:06,442 --> 00:08:08,096
and let them ferment.

145
00:08:08,226 --> 00:08:10,490
To do that, we built...

146
00:08:11,534 --> 00:08:12,840
this!

147
00:08:12,970 --> 00:08:14,972
- [Lea] We're going to
walk on top of these?

148
00:08:15,103 --> 00:08:16,147
- [Hiraku] Yeah!

149
00:08:16,278 --> 00:08:17,758
Make sure to stomp 'em
real good.

150
00:08:17,888 --> 00:08:19,716
- [Tia] I'm a little hesitant
to stomp on something

151
00:08:19,847 --> 00:08:21,370
that we're going to drink.

152
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:23,415
- [Hiraku] If you get tired,
you can switch with someone.

153
00:08:23,546 --> 00:08:25,287
- What about you?

154
00:08:25,417 --> 00:08:28,986
- Oh, me? I'm switching the
barrels as they fill up.

155
00:08:29,117 --> 00:08:30,858
By the way,
these barrels were built

156
00:08:30,988 --> 00:08:32,860
by the High Elf Lalasha
because she knows how to

157
00:08:32,990 --> 00:08:35,123
make containers
that are watertight.

158
00:08:36,341 --> 00:08:38,387
I had her make them right away.

159
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:40,520
All right, you guys
can start now!

160
00:08:40,650 --> 00:08:41,651
- [Lea] Uh...

161
00:08:43,044 --> 00:08:44,436
[grapes squishing]
[Lea yelping]

162
00:08:44,567 --> 00:08:47,004
Wow, you really sink into them.

163
00:08:47,135 --> 00:08:48,266
Am I doing it right?

164
00:08:48,397 --> 00:08:50,138
- Great, now let's see...

165
00:08:50,268 --> 00:08:53,533
Move in a circular motion
around the whole thing.

166
00:08:53,663 --> 00:08:55,709
- Okay!

167
00:08:55,839 --> 00:08:57,537
Let's go in this direction.

168
00:08:57,667 --> 00:08:59,016
- Okay.

169
00:08:59,147 --> 00:09:03,238
[Tia and Lea groaning anxiously]

170
00:09:03,368 --> 00:09:04,587
[Tia yelping]

171
00:09:04,718 --> 00:09:06,937
- Careful not to slip
and fall, Tia!

172
00:09:07,068 --> 00:09:08,286
- Okay!

173
00:09:08,417 --> 00:09:10,941
[Tia grunting]

174
00:09:11,072 --> 00:09:12,290
Oh, no!

175
00:09:12,421 --> 00:09:13,509
[Tia and Lea yelping]

176
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:14,902
[Hiraku gasping]
[water splashing]

177
00:09:15,032 --> 00:09:17,078
- [Hiraku] Are you all right?

178
00:09:17,208 --> 00:09:18,688
- I think so!

179
00:09:18,819 --> 00:09:20,647
[Tia and Lea sighing]

180
00:09:20,777 --> 00:09:21,735
- Sorry, Tia.

181
00:09:21,865 --> 00:09:23,693
I bumped into you.

182
00:09:23,824 --> 00:09:26,087
- Not at all, that was my fault.

183
00:09:27,436 --> 00:09:28,916
You know, this would be easier

184
00:09:29,046 --> 00:09:30,831
if we had a way
to keep our rhythm.

185
00:09:30,961 --> 00:09:33,573
It might keep all of
our movements in sync.

186
00:09:34,530 --> 00:09:35,575
- [Lea] Good point.

187
00:09:35,705 --> 00:09:38,012
[Leeta gasping excitedly]

188
00:09:38,142 --> 00:09:41,102
- I have an idea, we can use
that song we used to sing.

189
00:09:41,232 --> 00:09:44,061
It helped us before when
we worked in the village.

190
00:09:44,192 --> 00:09:45,106
- Oh, yeah!

191
00:09:45,236 --> 00:09:46,237
That just might work!

192
00:09:46,368 --> 00:09:47,717
- A song from your village?

193
00:09:47,848 --> 00:09:48,675
- Yeah, that's right!

194
00:09:48,805 --> 00:09:50,198
It goes like this!

195
00:09:51,286 --> 00:09:52,940
One, and two, three, go!

196
00:09:53,070 --> 00:09:57,466
[Leeta and Leely
singing in Elvish]

197
00:10:01,731 --> 00:10:05,779
[all singing in Elvish]
[hands tapping]

198
00:10:09,478 --> 00:10:12,568
[Tia yelping]

199
00:10:12,699 --> 00:10:14,091
[Tia laughing]

200
00:10:14,222 --> 00:10:16,006
[hands tapping]

201
00:10:16,137 --> 00:10:18,530
[grapes squishing]
[Tia laughing]

202
00:10:21,751 --> 00:10:24,580
- Looks like they
found their rhythm.

203
00:10:24,711 --> 00:10:26,060
- [Tia] Hey, Lu!

204
00:10:26,190 --> 00:10:28,671
Come on, it's really fun!

205
00:10:28,802 --> 00:10:29,846
- 'Kay.

206
00:10:29,977 --> 00:10:31,369
You're coming, too.
- Huh?

207
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:32,762
But I'm-
- [Lu] Let's go!

208
00:10:32,893 --> 00:10:34,459
- [Hiraku] Hey, wait!
- [Lu] Come on!

209
00:10:34,590 --> 00:10:37,071
[Hiraku yelping]
That's it!

210
00:10:37,201 --> 00:10:40,074
[all singing]

211
00:10:40,204 --> 00:10:42,380
[all laughing]

212
00:10:43,164 --> 00:10:44,165
[Hiraku sighing]

213
00:10:44,295 --> 00:10:46,123
- That was a lot of work today.

214
00:10:46,254 --> 00:10:49,649
- I'm exhausted,
but that was a lot of fun.

215
00:10:49,779 --> 00:10:52,739
- [Hiraku] Now, the yeast
on the skin of the grapes

216
00:10:52,869 --> 00:10:54,654
should ferment this for us.

217
00:10:56,133 --> 00:10:58,396
I wonder if we made too much.

218
00:10:58,527 --> 00:10:59,963
- I wouldn't worry about it.

219
00:11:00,094 --> 00:11:02,270
- I'm sure we'll have
no problem drinking it all.

220
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:03,358
- Totally!

221
00:11:03,488 --> 00:11:04,925
I can't wait to drink it!

222
00:11:05,055 --> 00:11:07,667
- Don't tell me
we didn't make enough!

223
00:11:07,797 --> 00:11:08,842
- [God] See?

224
00:11:08,972 --> 00:11:11,061
Look how much fun he's having!

225
00:11:11,192 --> 00:11:13,237
So can't you forgive me already?

226
00:11:13,368 --> 00:11:15,370
- Absolutely not!

227
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:18,199
You mistakenly punished
an innocent human soul,

228
00:11:18,329 --> 00:11:20,070
and then sneakily
tried to save him,

229
00:11:20,201 --> 00:11:21,681
only to end up sending him

230
00:11:21,811 --> 00:11:23,639
to the dreaded Forest of Death!

231
00:11:23,770 --> 00:11:24,727
[God flinching]

232
00:11:24,858 --> 00:11:26,250
And you gave him that spear!

233
00:11:26,381 --> 00:11:28,383
I can't believe you
gave him a replica

234
00:11:28,513 --> 00:11:30,080
of the Holy Lance Gryme!

235
00:11:30,211 --> 00:11:32,822
- Well, right now, he's only
using it as a farming tool.

236
00:11:32,953 --> 00:11:35,216
Plus, I got permission,
remember?

237
00:11:35,346 --> 00:11:36,347
- [Goddess] You didn't tell me

238
00:11:36,478 --> 00:11:37,784
you were giving that to a human!

239
00:11:37,914 --> 00:11:39,873
That thing will drain
all of their life force

240
00:11:40,003 --> 00:11:41,135
and kill them instantly!

241
00:11:41,265 --> 00:11:43,703
- But he's doing fine right now!

242
00:11:43,833 --> 00:11:46,618
I'm sure it's because he has
super fast recovery abilities

243
00:11:46,749 --> 00:11:49,317
since I gave him such a
healthy body this time around!

244
00:11:49,447 --> 00:11:51,667
- [Goddess] I'm telling you
that you were too careless!

245
00:11:51,798 --> 00:11:53,060
and besides that...

246
00:11:53,190 --> 00:11:54,888
And besides that!

247
00:11:57,020 --> 00:11:59,153
Why is the statue that's
supposed to me

248
00:11:59,283 --> 00:12:01,155
a grizzled old man?

249
00:12:01,285 --> 00:12:02,809
- [God] That is not my fault!

250
00:12:02,939 --> 00:12:04,375
- [Goddess] No excuses!

251
00:12:04,506 --> 00:12:07,030
As punishment, you will sit
like that for 300 years!

252
00:12:07,161 --> 00:12:10,120
- Please forgive me,
my daughter!

253
00:12:12,209 --> 00:12:15,299
[leaves rustling]

254
00:12:16,997 --> 00:12:18,868
[hammer tapping]

255
00:12:18,999 --> 00:12:21,436
[wolves growling]

256
00:12:21,566 --> 00:12:24,352
[Flora whimpering]

257
00:12:24,482 --> 00:12:26,702
- [Hiraku] I'm sensing
deja vu, here.

258
00:12:27,572 --> 00:12:28,269
- Flora?

259
00:12:28,399 --> 00:12:29,923
- My dear sister!

260
00:12:30,053 --> 00:12:32,099
- [Hiraku] They're
actually related?

261
00:12:32,752 --> 00:12:33,840
- [Flora] Yes!

262
00:12:33,970 --> 00:12:35,493
It was not long
after I figured out

263
00:12:35,624 --> 00:12:37,800
that you were being chased
by that black-hearted angel,

264
00:12:37,931 --> 00:12:39,846
I decided to follow you
all the way here.

265
00:12:39,976 --> 00:12:41,499
- Who did you say was
black-hearted?

266
00:12:41,630 --> 00:12:44,111
- [Flora] [yelps]
Why is she here?

267
00:12:44,241 --> 00:12:45,677
It was just an expression!

268
00:12:45,808 --> 00:12:49,464
- [Hiraku] Apparently,
Flora is also a vampire.

269
00:12:49,594 --> 00:12:50,595
And she's related to Lu.

270
00:12:50,726 --> 00:12:52,641
- Please, sister, help me!

271
00:12:52,772 --> 00:12:56,166
- Since you're already
here, why not relax

272
00:12:56,297 --> 00:12:57,733
and stay with us for a while?

273
00:12:57,864 --> 00:12:59,256
- Okay.

274
00:12:59,387 --> 00:13:01,998
I'm having a hard time
believing he's Lu's husband.

275
00:13:02,129 --> 00:13:04,261
Something feels off
about all this.

276
00:13:04,392 --> 00:13:05,610
[wolf growling]

277
00:13:05,741 --> 00:13:07,525
Ah, no, nevermind!

278
00:13:07,656 --> 00:13:09,353
- He's the one in charge here.

279
00:13:09,484 --> 00:13:11,878
And he's the master of
all these inferno wolves.

280
00:13:12,008 --> 00:13:14,315
He even took down
a giant wyvern!

281
00:13:14,445 --> 00:13:16,230
- I see now.

282
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:18,623
- I'm sorry for my behavior!

283
00:13:18,754 --> 00:13:20,103
- Don't worry about it.

284
00:13:20,234 --> 00:13:23,324
So anyways, you guys
are wolves, Kuro?

285
00:13:23,454 --> 00:13:25,500
I had no idea!
[Kuro growling]

286
00:13:25,630 --> 00:13:27,502
What's the inferno part mean?

287
00:13:27,632 --> 00:13:29,373
[fire roaring]

288
00:13:29,504 --> 00:13:31,549
Wow, that's amazing!

289
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:34,248
- You've been living
with them this whole time

290
00:13:34,378 --> 00:13:35,684
and didn't know?

291
00:13:35,815 --> 00:13:38,034
- I believe they're
well-known magical beasts.

292
00:13:38,165 --> 00:13:41,559
[Flora gasping excitedly]

293
00:13:42,778 --> 00:13:44,824
- You can think of this
as an apology.

294
00:13:44,954 --> 00:13:46,347
For Kuro and the wolves.

295
00:13:46,477 --> 00:13:48,349
We went ahead and
made dinner for you.

296
00:13:48,479 --> 00:13:50,133
[Flora munching happily]

297
00:13:50,264 --> 00:13:52,222
[Lu chuckling nervously]

298
00:13:52,353 --> 00:13:53,354
- [Flora] It's great!

299
00:13:53,484 --> 00:13:55,486
[sighs] This is fantastic!

300
00:13:55,617 --> 00:13:57,837
What's that soft, white stuff?

301
00:13:57,967 --> 00:13:59,664
- [Hiraku] Oh, that's
called tofu.

302
00:13:59,795 --> 00:14:02,319
After a lot of tries,
I finally got it right.

303
00:14:02,450 --> 00:14:04,539
- [Lu] It's made from
a bean called soybean.

304
00:14:04,669 --> 00:14:07,020
- [Flora] Wow, this is
made from beans?

305
00:14:07,150 --> 00:14:09,500
- Flavoring soup with salt
is fine and all,

306
00:14:09,631 --> 00:14:11,285
but I really wanted some miso.

307
00:14:11,415 --> 00:14:14,636
Plus, I wanted to be able to put
soy sauce on other stuff.

308
00:14:14,766 --> 00:14:16,768
- Miso? And soy sauce?

309
00:14:16,899 --> 00:14:18,509
- [Hiraku] Miso and
soy sauce are made

310
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:21,164
from fermented soybeans
and help to flavor food.

311
00:14:21,295 --> 00:14:22,862
- Fermented?

312
00:14:22,992 --> 00:14:26,300
- [Hiraku] Basically,
it seems in this world,

313
00:14:26,430 --> 00:14:28,737
fermented foods like
wine and cheese exist.

314
00:14:28,868 --> 00:14:31,696
However, they aren't aware
of the microorganisms

315
00:14:31,827 --> 00:14:34,090
that actually cause
fermentation.

316
00:14:34,221 --> 00:14:35,831
- I see.

317
00:14:35,962 --> 00:14:39,313
If tiny organisms we aren't able
to see with our eyes exist,

318
00:14:39,443 --> 00:14:40,923
and these same organisms
can cause

319
00:14:41,054 --> 00:14:43,491
transformations in matter
without magic,

320
00:14:43,621 --> 00:14:45,580
then that would serve
to explain all of this.

321
00:14:45,710 --> 00:14:47,799
- Come on, eat or talk, Flora.
- It seems that, like Lu,

322
00:14:47,930 --> 00:14:50,193
she's also passionate
about her research.

323
00:14:50,324 --> 00:14:54,458
- I have found a fascinating
new subject for my research!

324
00:14:54,589 --> 00:14:56,156
I will bring the wonders
of miso and soy sauce

325
00:14:56,286 --> 00:14:58,071
to all that I cross!

326
00:14:58,201 --> 00:14:59,594
And then there will
come a day when I will

327
00:14:59,724 --> 00:15:03,772
feast upon miso soup
and cold tofu forever!

328
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:05,339
- [Hiraku] After staying
a few days,

329
00:15:05,469 --> 00:15:07,471
Flora left with great haste
and excitement

330
00:15:07,602 --> 00:15:09,865
so she could make preparations
to move.

331
00:15:11,171 --> 00:15:13,216
- [Flora] I have returned!

332
00:15:13,347 --> 00:15:14,478
- Okay.

333
00:15:14,609 --> 00:15:16,176
- That was way faster
than I thought.

334
00:15:16,306 --> 00:15:18,439
You even brought
the maids with you.

335
00:15:20,267 --> 00:15:21,877
- Nice to meet you.

336
00:15:22,008 --> 00:15:24,532
My name is Anne, and I speak
on behalf of the other maids

337
00:15:24,662 --> 00:15:26,273
as their rep.

338
00:15:26,403 --> 00:15:28,710
We ask that you put us to use
as you so see fit, master.

339
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:32,279
- Uh, you don't really need
to be that formal.

340
00:15:32,409 --> 00:15:34,585
By the way, what are those?

341
00:15:34,716 --> 00:15:38,372
I mean, those are just
normal cows, right?

342
00:15:38,502 --> 00:15:39,808
- [Flora] That's right!

343
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:41,679
I made sure to bring
the right cows with me

344
00:15:41,810 --> 00:15:43,029
that would give us milk.

345
00:15:43,159 --> 00:15:44,508
- Oh!

346
00:15:44,639 --> 00:15:45,770
This is great!

347
00:15:45,901 --> 00:15:47,990
Now we can make
butter and cheese!

348
00:15:48,121 --> 00:15:50,166
[Tia humming thoughtfully]

349
00:15:56,694 --> 00:15:58,392
[Tia gasping]

350
00:15:58,522 --> 00:15:59,436
- [Tia] Excuse me!

351
00:15:59,567 --> 00:16:00,350
- What the-

352
00:16:00,481 --> 00:16:01,699
That's close!

353
00:16:01,830 --> 00:16:03,223
- I need to leave here
for a short while.

354
00:16:03,353 --> 00:16:04,441
- Sure.

355
00:16:04,572 --> 00:16:06,966
I wonder what she's
going off to do.

356
00:16:10,317 --> 00:16:11,753
[cow mooing]

357
00:16:11,883 --> 00:16:13,407
- I have now returned!

358
00:16:13,537 --> 00:16:15,104
- Okay.

359
00:16:15,235 --> 00:16:17,628
- And I have brought my
underlings here with me as well!

360
00:16:17,759 --> 00:16:19,804
- My name is Granmaria.

361
00:16:20,544 --> 00:16:22,155
- I'm Kudel.

362
00:16:22,285 --> 00:16:25,375
- I'm Corone, it's a pleasure
to finally meet you.

363
00:16:25,506 --> 00:16:28,813
- I'm Daga, the representative
of the lizardmen.

364
00:16:28,944 --> 00:16:30,946
- Also... I've prepared
this as well!

365
00:16:31,077 --> 00:16:32,861
[chicken clucking]
It's a chicken!

366
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:34,428
- Does it breathe fire?

367
00:16:34,558 --> 00:16:35,603
- It does not.

368
00:16:35,733 --> 00:16:36,952
- What about eggs?

369
00:16:37,083 --> 00:16:38,171
- It lays them!

370
00:16:38,301 --> 00:16:39,563
That's great.

371
00:16:41,826 --> 00:16:43,437
[Tia laughs happily]
Thanks to everyone here,

372
00:16:43,567 --> 00:16:46,135
this place got
a lot more civilized.

373
00:16:47,441 --> 00:16:49,443
- For the rooms on
this side, Lamulias,

374
00:16:49,573 --> 00:16:52,098
I want them dusted before
we wash the floors.

375
00:16:52,228 --> 00:16:54,796
- Understood, Miss.

376
00:16:54,926 --> 00:16:56,450
- Oh, sorry for interrupting.

377
00:16:56,580 --> 00:16:57,668
- It's fine.

378
00:16:57,799 --> 00:16:58,800
- [Hiraku] The maids
that arrived

379
00:16:58,930 --> 00:17:00,715
belong to a race of ogres.

380
00:17:00,845 --> 00:17:03,239
I guess it's to be expected
since they're professionals,

381
00:17:03,370 --> 00:17:04,632
but as soon as they showed up,

382
00:17:04,762 --> 00:17:07,243
all our chores got done
a lot faster.

383
00:17:07,374 --> 00:17:10,899
However, the inhabitants
of this world

384
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:13,902
don't seem to cook any
complicated dishes.

385
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:16,383
I tried to teach them
all the different methods

386
00:17:16,513 --> 00:17:17,645
of cooking that I knew.

387
00:17:17,775 --> 00:17:18,515
Dressing salads!

388
00:17:18,646 --> 00:17:19,473
Steaming!

389
00:17:19,603 --> 00:17:21,170
- [Maids] Ah!

390
00:17:21,301 --> 00:17:23,042
- [Hiraku] It seems like I got
them interested in cooking

391
00:17:23,172 --> 00:17:24,652
all at once.

392
00:17:24,782 --> 00:17:25,783
[knife tapping]

393
00:17:25,914 --> 00:17:27,307
- [Anne] Dinner is served.

394
00:17:27,437 --> 00:17:29,309
Today, I tried making
a dish of killer rabbit

395
00:17:29,439 --> 00:17:30,701
with fragrant vegetables.

396
00:17:30,832 --> 00:17:32,268
- Oh, wow.

397
00:17:32,399 --> 00:17:34,618
So those things are called
killer rabbits, huh?

398
00:17:36,664 --> 00:17:38,274
This looks wild.

399
00:17:38,405 --> 00:17:41,756
They're all very strong,
despite their appearances.

400
00:17:41,886 --> 00:17:45,151
They display both proper manners
and a bit of power.

401
00:17:46,456 --> 00:17:48,328
Then there are the
angels that Tia brought.

402
00:17:48,458 --> 00:17:50,286
- Now then, you're all to patrol

403
00:17:50,417 --> 00:17:52,158
a different region
of the forest.

404
00:17:52,288 --> 00:17:54,725
- [Hiraku] Granmaria,
Kudel, and Corone.

405
00:17:54,856 --> 00:17:56,684
I was wondering why
they all showed up

406
00:17:56,814 --> 00:17:58,468
in such serious-looking armor.

407
00:17:58,599 --> 00:18:00,383
It seems that after
the wyvern attack,

408
00:18:00,514 --> 00:18:02,124
Tia planned on
having them act as

409
00:18:02,255 --> 00:18:03,995
our security on the premises.

410
00:18:04,126 --> 00:18:05,910
I feel safer having them around.

411
00:18:06,041 --> 00:18:08,043
The lizardmen are
in charge of all labor

412
00:18:08,174 --> 00:18:09,958
that requires strength outdoors.

413
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:11,960
Thanks to them,
our construction work

414
00:18:12,091 --> 00:18:14,397
is moving even faster now.

415
00:18:14,528 --> 00:18:16,486
By the way, I had
their leader, Daga,

416
00:18:16,617 --> 00:18:19,054
tie a scarf around his arm.

417
00:18:19,185 --> 00:18:21,317
I feel bad, but I'm not able to
tell them apart otherwise.

418
00:18:21,448 --> 00:18:23,711
- I guess that does
make sense in a way.

419
00:18:23,841 --> 00:18:25,843
- Now that I think about it,

420
00:18:25,974 --> 00:18:28,977
this place is really filling up
with people living here.

421
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:31,066
How many of us are there?

422
00:18:31,197 --> 00:18:33,199
[graph beeping]

423
00:18:33,329 --> 00:18:34,330
A lot.

424
00:18:34,461 --> 00:18:36,071
- [Lea] Hiraku!

425
00:18:36,202 --> 00:18:37,333
I brought all the elves

426
00:18:37,464 --> 00:18:39,074
that were still
wandering the forest!

427
00:18:39,205 --> 00:18:40,597
- [Hiraku] Oh?

428
00:18:42,208 --> 00:18:44,035
Now there are even more?

429
00:18:44,166 --> 00:18:45,211
So are they all women?

430
00:18:45,341 --> 00:18:46,429
Where are the men?

431
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:48,344
I don't see them.

432
00:18:48,475 --> 00:18:50,912
- There weren't really any men
who survived the human war.

433
00:18:51,042 --> 00:18:52,479
- Oh, wow.

434
00:18:52,609 --> 00:18:54,611
- But that's okay, really.

435
00:18:54,742 --> 00:18:57,484
We can just start making
lots more now!

436
00:18:57,614 --> 00:18:59,094
[elves cheering]

437
00:18:59,225 --> 00:19:00,791
- I hope that works out for you!

438
00:19:00,922 --> 00:19:04,012
I decided not to ask them
how they planned to do it.

439
00:19:05,666 --> 00:19:07,668
- Hey, what's going on here?

440
00:19:07,798 --> 00:19:09,148
- Who knows?

441
00:19:09,278 --> 00:19:10,932
I'm just here because
I was asked to come.

442
00:19:11,062 --> 00:19:12,455
- He said to gather

443
00:19:12,586 --> 00:19:14,283
all the different
representatives here today.

444
00:19:14,414 --> 00:19:17,634
- I wonder if some sort of
terrible problem has arisen.

445
00:19:17,765 --> 00:19:18,940
- [Hiraku] Hey.

446
00:19:20,202 --> 00:19:22,509
Sorry for calling you all
here like this.

447
00:19:22,639 --> 00:19:25,729
There's something I wanna
talk about with all of you.

448
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:26,817
[all humming questioningly]

449
00:19:26,948 --> 00:19:28,428
Here's the thing.

450
00:19:28,558 --> 00:19:30,386
I want a name for our home here.

451
00:19:30,517 --> 00:19:32,040
- You mean this place?

452
00:19:32,171 --> 00:19:33,215
The farm?

453
00:19:33,346 --> 00:19:34,434
- [Hiraku] Yeah.

454
00:19:34,564 --> 00:19:36,218
At first, it was just
my little hut

455
00:19:36,349 --> 00:19:37,611
and some crop fields,

456
00:19:37,741 --> 00:19:39,395
but then more buildings
started popping up,

457
00:19:39,526 --> 00:19:41,354
and more people
started moving in.

458
00:19:41,484 --> 00:19:43,573
It's like a village now, right?

459
00:19:43,704 --> 00:19:46,837
That's why I wanna come up
with a name for this village.

460
00:19:46,968 --> 00:19:48,535
- I like that idea!

461
00:19:48,665 --> 00:19:50,798
A name for our very own village!

462
00:19:50,928 --> 00:19:52,408
Can't we just name it after you,

463
00:19:52,539 --> 00:19:55,063
since you're the original
founder of the whole place?

464
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:56,804
- [Hiraku] No.

465
00:19:56,934 --> 00:19:59,154
Then it'd be something like
Hiraku Village or Machio Town.

466
00:19:59,285 --> 00:20:01,200
I don't really like
the sound of that.

467
00:20:01,330 --> 00:20:02,723
- In that case, then,

468
00:20:02,853 --> 00:20:05,291
how about we name it
after the forest we're in?

469
00:20:05,421 --> 00:20:07,075
- That sounds like a good idea!

470
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:09,556
By the way, what is
this forest called?

471
00:20:09,686 --> 00:20:11,035
- It's the Forest of Death.

472
00:20:11,166 --> 00:20:12,907
- For real? That's scary.

473
00:20:13,037 --> 00:20:14,604
- [Tia] So the Village of Death?

474
00:20:14,735 --> 00:20:16,215
- [Lu] Sounds like a ghost town!

475
00:20:16,345 --> 00:20:17,912
- [Hiraku] It sounds like
it'd have a poisoned swamp.

476
00:20:19,653 --> 00:20:20,828
What is it?

477
00:20:22,743 --> 00:20:24,962
You mean this door, here?

478
00:20:25,093 --> 00:20:26,529
You want me to open it?

479
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:32,143
[Hiraku grunting]
[door creaking]

480
00:20:33,710 --> 00:20:35,103
The Great Tree Village!

481
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:37,236
[all humming happily]

482
00:20:39,238 --> 00:20:42,153
[sentimental music]

483
00:20:45,069 --> 00:20:47,246
[fire crackling]

484
00:20:47,376 --> 00:20:48,943
Hello, everyone!

485
00:20:49,073 --> 00:20:53,077
From now on, this place is
the Great Tree Village!

486
00:20:53,208 --> 00:20:57,386
In celebration of this day,
we're going to have a party!

487
00:20:57,517 --> 00:20:58,909
[all cheering]

488
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:01,782
And no party would be
complete without this!

489
00:21:01,912 --> 00:21:03,523
The first batch of wine
we made here

490
00:21:03,653 --> 00:21:05,786
in the Great Tree Village!

491
00:21:05,916 --> 00:21:08,832
Everyone, enjoy yourselves!

492
00:21:10,486 --> 00:21:12,009
- [Leeta and Leely]
Mayor Hiraku!

493
00:21:12,140 --> 00:21:14,055
- Mayor!
[wolf howling]

494
00:21:14,185 --> 00:21:15,404
[Flora whistling]

495
00:21:15,535 --> 00:21:17,058
- Wait!

496
00:21:17,188 --> 00:21:20,017
No, that's something we need
to decide later, as a group!

497
00:21:20,148 --> 00:21:21,932
- What are you talking about?

498
00:21:22,063 --> 00:21:23,847
You're the only one for the job.

499
00:21:23,978 --> 00:21:25,109
- She's right.

500
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:27,155
They're already
calling you mayor!

501
00:21:27,286 --> 00:21:29,375
- [Crowd] Mayor Hiraku!

502
00:21:29,505 --> 00:21:30,550
Mayor Hiraku!

503
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:32,726
- I see.
- [Crowd] Mayor Hiraku!

504
00:21:32,856 --> 00:21:34,554
Mayor Hiraku!

505
00:21:34,684 --> 00:21:36,643
Mayor Hiraku!

506
00:21:36,773 --> 00:21:40,560
[crowd cheering]
[Hiraku laughing]

507
00:21:46,653 --> 00:21:47,958
[mugs clanking]

508
00:21:48,089 --> 00:21:51,310
[sentimental music]

509
00:22:06,934 --> 00:22:09,153
[Lu sighing]

510
00:22:10,372 --> 00:22:13,201
[crowd murmuring]

511
00:22:14,637 --> 00:22:16,117
[Tia gasping]

512
00:22:16,247 --> 00:22:18,815
[Hiraku humming questioningly]

513
00:22:18,946 --> 00:22:20,164
[Tia grunting]
[hand tapping]

514
00:22:20,295 --> 00:22:23,516
[Tia humming]
[hand tapping rapidly]

515
00:22:23,646 --> 00:22:26,170
["Feel the winds"
by Yui Hizuki plays]

516
00:22:26,301 --> 00:22:28,303
- You're a little drunk
there, huh?

517
00:22:28,434 --> 00:22:29,783
- What's the matter, Hiraku?

518
00:22:29,913 --> 00:22:32,133
You're sitting all by
yourself, zoning out.

519
00:22:32,263 --> 00:22:34,265
- Nothing.

520
00:22:34,396 --> 00:22:36,050
Nothing's the matter.

521
00:22:36,180 --> 00:22:38,444
I was just thinking about
how happy I am.

522
00:22:38,574 --> 00:22:40,663
That this all feels
like a dream.

523
00:22:42,230 --> 00:22:44,014
- This isn't a dream.

524
00:22:44,145 --> 00:22:47,931
All of us will keep living
together, enjoying life.

525
00:22:48,976 --> 00:22:50,847
- Yeah, you're right.

526
00:22:50,978 --> 00:22:52,109
I'd like that.

527
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:53,546
- Yeah?

528
00:22:55,504 --> 00:22:58,638
Let's toast to
the Great Tree Village!

529
00:22:59,813 --> 00:23:01,249
- Yeah!

530
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:03,860
- [Hiraku And Tia] Cheers!
[mugs tapping]

531
00:23:04,774 --> 00:23:06,863
- [yawns] No fair!

532
00:23:06,994 --> 00:23:09,649
I'm gonna toast, too,
you black-hearted angel!

533
00:23:09,779 --> 00:23:11,128
- Seriously?

534
00:23:11,259 --> 00:23:12,913
You were pretending to sleep
this whole time?

535
00:23:13,043 --> 00:23:14,480
- [Lu] Come on!

536
00:23:14,610 --> 00:23:16,395
- Very well, then.

537
00:23:18,222 --> 00:23:19,702
- How many years has it been?

538
00:23:19,833 --> 00:23:21,008
- [Tia And Lu] Cheers!

539
00:23:21,138 --> 00:23:22,575
It's been a while
since I've had wine.

540
00:23:22,705 --> 00:23:24,011
It tastes better
than I remember.

541
00:23:24,141 --> 00:23:25,404
- Gimme another!

542
00:23:25,534 --> 00:23:29,625
[crowd cheering and laughing]

543
00:23:39,505 --> 00:23:42,769
- I guess I'll give it
a shot as mayor.

544
00:23:47,687 --> 00:23:51,125
[rustic music playing]

